          "general_description": "ARC-AGI-2 assesses AI performance on coloured-grid transformation problems. Worked input-output examples precede new inputs for which the AI must produce output grids. The developers connect this task to learning new rules, abstract reasoning and broader intelligence. The release contains 1,000 development problems and public, semi-private and private evaluation sets of 120 problems each. Human solving data informed selection and matching of evaluation-set difficulty. This review concerns the public evaluation problems, official scoring software and ARC Prize’s verified-evaluation rules. Two attempts are allowed per new input, with credit requiring an exact grid match. The software averages input success within problems and then averages problem scores. Verified evaluations specify settings and a spending limit and use one run. Public materials support inspection and development; hidden-set access is controlled. No AI norm tables, validated skill subscales or formal user qualifications are supplied in this passage."
        },
        "part_B": {
